From 0f78dcd6bb8fb5dd5f8f5630a8a7515b9b42f7f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Azra Bano <azrabano.work@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 00:24:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Warn when a linesearch uses all ls_iterations.

A CG or Newton linesearch that exhausts ls_iterations without improvement
ends the solve silently, at a point that is not the minimizer (#3628).

Add mjWARN_LINESEARCH, raised after the constraint solve when any recorded
iteration's linesearch used all ls_iterations evaluations. The check reads the
solver statistics in the serial part of the forward pass, since islands can be
solved in parallel. A linesearch that runs out of evaluations without
improvement is now recorded as an iteration with zero improvement, so that it
is visible in mjData.solver and to the check.
